    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Confirm that $x=3$ and $x=2$ are both solutions of the equation $x+\\frac{6}{x}=5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both values give $5$, so both are solutions.",
      "worked": "For $x=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{6}{x}&=3+\\frac{6}{3}\\\\x+\\frac{6}{x}&=3+2\\\\x+\\frac{6}{x}&=5\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac{6}{x}&=2+\\frac{6}{2}\\\\x+\\frac{6}{x}&=2+3\\\\x+\\frac{6}{x}&=5\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy the equation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 82
  },
